    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n$x = 3 - 3t, y = 2(t + 2)^{3} - 2, - ∞ < t < ∞$.\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/value": "t =-6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "81c8b4e9-6f15-57ce-8d11-bb4d14691433"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t = 1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "fccc2e1d-9729-5d8f-8aee-258413419724"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t =-2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "8a544916-806f-5eb2-86a6-6558a73b782f"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t = 6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "d30a18bd-f817-5f4d-b7cb-c1c2e466c8cb"
            },
            {
              ":answer/value": "t =-1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/id": "0a9f0ab5-9baa-5645-810f-7bd1d3cbb6c1"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/id": "61d9371e-3f06-50e3-aa86-77c7894ac2bb",
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "8a544916-806f-5eb2-86a6-6558a73b782f"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if $y'(t)=0$ while $x'(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=-3,\\qquad y'(t)=6{t}^{2}+24t+24.\n$$\n\nSolving $y'(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2}+24t+24 & =0 \\\\ 6(t+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(-2) & =-3\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=-2$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "5107a7a4-8fae-5577-9194-5eec8c42d8f0"
    },
